  "confounders": [
    "GEOLOCATION PROMPT (stated confounder, prompt state not observed). squallar-location's gate asks at startup on a fresh origin (LocationMemo default enabled=true, attempts=0; permission Prompt -> request_location -> watchPosition), and each automation session starts on empty website data, so Safari was asked for location on this leg. Nobody was at the Mac to see or answer a prompt. `leg_liveness` shows it stalled nothing. A `squallar.location` = {\"attempts\":2,\"enabled\":true} seed avoids it; not used.",
    "Before any Mac leg, a 12-day-old Safari `--automation` process (pid 5711) made every session time out pairing; it was killed and safaridriver launched a fresh automation Safari.",
    "Served from the Linux box through an ssh reverse tunnel at http://127.0.0.1:<port> on the Mac (a secure context, so COOP/COEP give cross-origin isolation with no certificate on the Mac). The app bundle and the beacons crossed the tunnel; the app's data fetches went from the Mac to the internet directly.",
    "WALL is a FLOOR: every calibrate run reached the 4 GiB policy cap (4096 MiB touched and alive), and one wasm32 memory cannot exceed 4 GiB, so this Mac's kill point was not reached.",
    "Display: KVM on the Mac, real 3440x1440 panel (devicePixelRatio 1); a 1920x1080 display was also online. App backend BrowserWebGpu.",
    "Served build: app b92a784f7 (wasm sha256 in provenance); rig at the `commit` column.",
    "Driven route missed ticks: 50 driven against 73 beaconed, and the last census differs (driven 624921651 B, beaconed 657647417 B). This leg logged ~103k `overlay/model ... off the frame` lines and the page's 1200-entry console ring turned over faster than the 2 s scrape; the beaconed log is the complete record. Ceilings, wall and every other column agree."
  ],
